# While macOS reports memory pressure Cra keeps no page made ahead (SparePage.keeps): the sweep closes
# the spare, and the next tab makes its own page. Once pressure reads normal again, the refill after
# a tab makes a spare and the tab after takes it. The pressure is held with memoryPressure=, not read
# from the Mac, so a full Mac running the scenario (a simulator beside it) doesn't make it fail.
budget rss=900 stalls50=8
cra://debug?memoryPressure=normal
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
wait 4
cra://debug?memoryPressure=warning
expect-log spare pages: dropped 1 for memory pressure warning
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=two
wait 4
reject-log takes a spare page
cra://debug?memoryPressure=normal
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=three
wait 4
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=four
expect-log takes a spare page
cra://debug?memoryPressure=system
reject-log fault:
